<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a> has been approved by Chinese regulators, opening the door for the AI system to reach iPhones in the country for the first time.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2024/09/apple-intelligence-black.jpeg" alt="" width="1400" height="788" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-963902" /><br/>
<a href="https://www.reuters.com/technology/apple-intelligence-ai-service-registered-with-chinas-cyberspace-regulator-2026-07-15/"><em>Reuters</em></a> reports that China's Cyberspace Administration registered Apple's on-device generative AI service this week, putting it on a list of newly cleared providers that also includes homegrown systems from Chinese phone makers.<br/>
<br/>
An unnamed source told the outlet that Apple's AI features in the country will draw on models from both Baidu and Alibaba. <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/02/14/apple-intelligence-plan-for-china-report/">In February 2025</a>, Alibaba was reported to be building the primary system and Baidu contributing on a smaller scale.<br/>
<br/>
Alibaba confirmed its part of the arrangement directly, telling <em>Reuters</em> that its Qwen model will power &zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj; functions across iOS, iPadOS, macOS, and visionOS for Chinese users, including both text and image generation. No launch date has been given, though approval typically precedes a rollout by only a few months, putting a China debut roughly in line with Apple's usual fall software release cycle.<br/>
<br/>
Apple actually <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/03/30/apple-intelligence-china-mistake/">briefly switched the features on early</a> for some Chinese users back in March, months ahead of getting the green light, and a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/11/25/apple-intelligence-feedback-form-china/">feedback form aimed at Chinese users</a> appeared on Apple's site late last year as the company inched closer to approval.<br/>
<br/>
iPhone shipments in China <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/14/iphone-17-pricing-helped-apple-china-q2-26/">climbed 24.4 percent year-over-year</a> in the second quarter, making Apple the fastest-growing smartphone brand in a market that otherwise kept shrinking. A working version of &zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj; could help sustain that momentum, though Apple is still catching up to domestic rivals that built AI features into their phones well before it did.<div class="linkback">Tags: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/china/">China</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/15/apple-intelligence-cleared-to-launch-in-china/">Apple Intelligence Finally Cleared to Launch in China</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/apple-intelligence-finally-cleared-to-launch-in-china.2485413/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>